<title>JAPAN: Showa Shell operating rates rise in 1996.</title>
<headline>Showa Shell operating rates rise in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The operating rates of Showa Shell Sekiyu KK's refineries rose to an average 86.9 percent in 1996, up from 84.1 percent in the previous year, a company spokesman said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The figures include the operating rates of Showa Shell's group firms, Showa Yokkaichi Sekiyu Co Ltd, Toa Oil Co Ltd and Seibu Oil Co Ltd, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>Showa Shell Sekiyu KK, an oil refiner and distributor, is owned 50 percent by the Royal Dutch/Shell Group.</p>
</text>
